From 520395548a0e59eaf576a7ec024dce44a483fd77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott J Guyton <kiljoy001@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:52:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Bound every declared count and length by the bytes that
 remain

Each section and function body declares its length before its contents, so
nothing is read past the end of the one being read, a section is checked to
end where it said it would, and no count claims more entries than there are
bytes left for them. Vectors are read into arrays sized by those checked
counts. A data count is bounded by what is left of the module, and a function
declares at most 50,000 locals, the limit the JavaScript API sets.

A 141-byte module could previously make either reader allocate or loop by a
count of hundreds of millions.
